 ## [Unreleased]
 
 ### Added
+- `network/finding-kb.json`: a **finding knowledge base** keyed by classifier `rule_id` — a remediation entry (category, title, why, read-only *how-to-test* commands, *how-to-fix* steps, references) for every one of the 199 non-low built-in rule_ids. Loaded by `network/report.py` (`_load_finding_kb`, env override `ARANUM_FINDING_KB`); a custom or generic-fallback rule falls back to a service→category map. Guidance commands are templates (`<host>`/`<port>`/`<service>`/…) and never execute; *test* steps are read-only confirmation only.
+- `network/report.py`: findings now carry additive `category` / `kb_id` / `kb_match` (`"rule"` | `"service-default"` | `""`) attached at finalize time, and reports gain a **"Top risks by category"** section grouping non-low findings by KB category and class with their Why / How-to-test / How-to-fix / References. The smb relay-vs-fileservice split keys a host's category on whether it also exposes Kerberos (88) or LDAP (389).
+- `network/report-dashboard.py`: an **Active Directory** page (detected domain controllers + AD findings grouped by attack-path family, with an "Uncorrelated signals" caveat since domain identity is not yet established), a **Categories** page (findings by KB category with inline test/fix guidance), a **Run health** panel (dispatcher `[!]` warnings that no rule grades — tool-missing/refused/timeout/error coverage gaps, not findings), and per-finding KB guidance expanders with copy-to-clipboard command buttons.
+- `aranumtoolkit/data-sources.json`: `finding-knowledge-base` provenance entry for `network/finding-kb.json` (owner, refresh policy, required-keys derivation).
 - `standalones/passwords/password-scrape.sh` + `standalones/passwords/Get-WeakPassword.ps1`: cross-platform read-only password/secret **compliance scanner** for shell history and logs. Two detection banks — weak-password shapes (`Password1!`, keyboard walks incl. shifted, season/month+year, sequences, repeats, leet, base words) and secret/credential "key terms" (command-line password flags, `mysql -p`, `sshpass`, `net user`, `ConvertTo-SecureString -AsPlainText`, 40+ secret env vars, provider API keys/tokens AWS/GitHub/Slack/Google/Stripe/Twilio/SendGrid/OpenAI/npm, JWTs, private-key headers, URL/DB connection strings with creds, Authorization headers, generic `key=secret` assignments). `--history`/`-History` sweeps standard bash/zsh/PSReadLine history + common text logs; `--weak-only`/`--secrets-only` bank selection; TAB/CSV output to an operator path; exit 1 on findings for CI compliance gates.
 - `standalones/proxy/connect-reply-sim.py`: scapy-based HTTP **CONNECT reply simulator** — crafts the `HTTP/1.1 200 Connection Established` TCP segment a remote host/proxy returns, for exercising clients/`--proxy` routing/monitoring in a lab. Dry-run by default (prints packet / writes pcap); transmit gated behind an explicit `--send` flag per §9.1. `--sniff-respond` lab-responder mode derives seq/ack from an observed CONNECT.
 - `standalones/passwords/Get-WeakPassword.cmd`: double-click / console launcher for the Windows password scanner — per-process `-ExecutionPolicy Bypass` (nothing system-wide changed), prefers PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`) then in-box Windows PowerShell 5.1, passes arguments through, keeps the window open on a double-click. Fixes the "double-clicking the .ps1 just opens a document viewer" problem.
